    "title": "Tottenham vs. Atletico Madrid Lineups, Predictions, UEFA Champions League Live Streaming, How & Where to Watch",
    "text": "Tottenham Hotspur will play Atletico Madrid at the Tottenham Hotspur Stadium for the second leg of the Champions League Round of 16 today.Both teams played in their respective leagues over the weekend, with both teams pulling positive results.AdvertisementTottenham Hotspur ended their losing streak in the Premier League and drew 1-1 with Liverpool. Spurs were losing 1-0 to Liverpool since the first half, but Richarlison scored the equalizer in the 90th minute to gain a point at Anfield.Atletico Madrid defeated Getafe 1-0 at home in La Liga with a goal from Nahuel Molina. Atletico's win pushes them 3rd in the La Liga table with 57 points, and they are 13 points behind league leaders FC Barcelona.Last week, Atletico Madrid defeated Tottenham Hotspur 5-2 in the first leg of the Champions League Round of 16. Marcos Llorente, Antoine Griezmann, Robin Le Normand, and Julian Alvarez, who scored two goals, were the goal scorers for Atletico Madrid.AdvertisementAntoine Griezmann of Atletico de Madrid celebrates scoring his team's second goal during the UEFA Champions League 2025/26 Round of 16 First Leg match between Atletico de Madrid and Tottenham Hotspur FC at Estadio Civitas Metropolitano on March 10, 2026 in Madrid, Spain. (Photo by Juan Manuel Serrano Arce/Getty Images)Photo by Juan Manuel Serrano Arce/Getty Images (Photo by Juan Manuel Serrano Arce&sol;Getty Images)Spurs need to score at least three goals for a chance to compete against Atletico Madrid and reach the quarterfinals.Official Lineups for Tottenham Hotspur and Atletico MadridTottenham Hotspur Goalkeeper: Guglielmo VicarioDefenders: Djed Spence, Radu Dragusin, Micky Van De Ven, Cristian Romero, Pedro PorroMidfielders: Archie Gray, Pape Sarr, Xavi SimonsForwards: Mathys Tel, Randal Kolo MuaniAtletico MadridGoalkeeper: Juan MussoDefenders: Matteo Ruggeri, David Hancko, Robin Le Normand, Nahuel MolinaMidfielders: Ademola Lookman, Johnny Cardoso, Marcos Llorente, Giuliano SimeoneForwards: Julian Alvarez, Antoine GriezmannWhere to Watch Tottenham Hotspur vs Atletico Madrid - 2nd Leg Champions League Round of 16The second leg of Tottenham Hotspur vs Atletico Madrid will kick off at 4 p.m. ET/ 1 p.m. PT in the United States.The match will kick off at 8 p.m. local time at the Tottenham Hotspur Stadium in London, England. The match will be available to watch in the U.S. and in other countries through select TV channels and streaming services.AdvertisementDAZN US (USA)Paramount+ (USA)TNT Sports 3 (UK)Movistar Plus+ (Spain)Prediction: Tottenham 1-2 Atletico Madrid (Tottenham 3-7 Atletico Madrid Aggregate Score) Atletico Madrid Advances to Champions League QuarterfinalThis story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 18, 2026, where it first appeared in the Soccer section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
